# Communication Rules
- Always start messages with "Hoo"
- Be concise and clear in responses
- Provide explanations for suggested changes

# Code Style Rules
- Use Swift and SwiftUI for all iOS development
- Follow Apple's Swift API Design Guidelines
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use proper indentation (4 spaces)

# Documentation Rules
- Add debug logs for important operations
- Include comments explaining complex logic
- Document public interfaces and methods
- Use // MARK: for code section organization

# SwiftUI Best Practices
- Use PreviewProvider for all Views
- Keep View files under 300 lines when possible
- Extract reusable components into separate views
- Use proper view modifiers ordering

# Project Structure
- Organize code by feature modules
- Keep resources in appropriate folders
- Follow MVVM architecture pattern
- Use MVVM repository architecture with Dependency Injection
- Separate business logic from UI code

# Testing Rules
- Write unit tests for business logic
- Include UI tests for critical flows
- Use meaningful test names
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
